# TowerOS Global Rules

Multi-tenant SaaS on the TowerOS codebase. **Active modules: Ticketing (`ticketing`), E-Forms (`e_approval`, backend `EApproval`), DocExtract (`doc_extract`), Document Control (`document_register`, backend `Documents` module, `ControlledDocument*` classes, frontend `controlled-documents-api.ts`).** Work only in these four and the shared `core` / `team_access` plumbing they need. AiAssistant, Help, Billing beyond what the four active modules need, and the platform/tenancy/identity/admin/workspace plumbing stay untouched unless asked.
Document Control and E-Forms call each other (`ControlledDocumentEApprovalHookService`, `UpgradeIsoFormForRevisionsCommand`). The lease/permit feature (module key `documents`) lives in the same backend `Documents` module as Document Control.
Module gating: the platform list is `TOWEROS_TENANT_ENABLED_MODULES` (comma-separated, parsed in `config/toweros.php`). A tenant's `enabled_modules` can only narrow it. `core` and `team_access` are always on. The product set is `core,team_access,e_approval,ticketing,doc_extract,document_register`. Verified enforcement: the `tenant.module` route middleware returns 403 and is applied to `doc_extract`, `billings`, `ai_assistant`, `documents`, and `document_register`. Ticketing and E-Forms are not route-gated, so switching them off hides navigation and (via `TenantModuleRbacSyncService` / `TenantRbacPermissionCatalog`) removes permissions. Run `/audit-module-gating` for the remaining unknowns.
Users: agents/staff working tickets, e-form submitters and approvers, document controllers, tenant admins, platform admins.

## Repo map (repo root = TowerOS)
- `backend/` Laravel 13.7, PHP 8.3.
  - `app/Core/*` shared base: Contracts, Events, Exceptions, Http, Jobs, Models (`BaseModel`), Services (`AbstractDomainService`), Repositories (`AbstractEloquentRepository`), Support.
  - Ticketing models live in `app/Models/` (`TicketingTicket`, `TicketingComment`, `TicketingAttachment`, `TicketingLink`), next to `User` and `Tenant`. EApproval, Documents and DocExtract models live in that module's `Models/` folder. Put a new model where that module already puts them.
  - `app/Modules/<Module>/` holds `Http/Controllers/V1`, `Services`, `Support`, `Notifications` (see `Modules/Ticketing`). Controllers extend `AbstractApiController`.
  - Routes in `routes/api/v1`. Central migrations in `database/migrations`, tenant migrations in `database/migrations/tenant`.
  - Tests in `tests/{Feature,Unit,Support}` (PHPUnit 12, helpers in `tests/Support/Concerns`).
- `frontend/` Next.js 16.2 (App Router, no `src/` folder), React 19, Tailwind 4.
  - Routes: `app/(platform|public|print|request-focus)/<route>`. UI: `components/<area>` (base primitives, tables and pickers in `components/ui`, shadcn/base-ui + class-variance-authority). Feature helpers: `lib/<area>` (for example `lib/ticketing`).
  - API: one client per audience in `lib/api` — `client.ts` (tenant), `central-client.ts` (platform admin), `public-tenant-client.ts` (public pages) — plus `error.ts`, `paginated.ts`, and one `lib/api/modules/<module>-api.ts` per module. Shared shapes in `modules/<module>/types.ts`. State: `stores/` (zustand). Hooks: `hooks/`.
- `services/doc-extract/` Python service behind the DocExtract module.
- `docker/`, `scripts/`, `.github/workflows/`, `docs/`.
- Docs are the source of truth. Read the matching one before changing a module or the UI system: `docs/Rules`, `docs/design-system`, `docs/architecture`, `docs/modules`, `docs/frontend`, `docs/local-dev`, `docs/ops`.

## Stack in use (do not add libraries without asking)
- Backend: Sanctum + Passport, Socialite (Microsoft Azure SSO), WebAuthn (`packages/lbuchs-webauthn`), Spatie Permission 7 + Activitylog, stancl/tenancy 3.10 (database-per-tenant), Horizon + Predis, Soketi (Pusher protocol), Stripe, AWS SDK, Pint. Redis 7 for cache/queue. Tests: PHPUnit. No static analyser or Pest is installed.
- Frontend: TanStack Query + Table, react-hook-form + zod 4, zustand, axios, next-themes, shadcn (radix-ui + @base-ui/react), recharts, laravel-echo + pusher-js, Vitest, ESLint. No Prettier, Playwright, i18n or URL-state library is installed.

## Deployment
- Production: AWS EC2 + RDS MySQL 8.4 (baseline), ECS Fargate is the scale path.
- Hostnames (DNS A records — no IP address in these rules): `app`, `appmenu`, `console`, `staging` under `.alliancetowers.com`.
- API: `api.alliancetowers.com` via CloudFront, origin nginx on the EC2 host.
- Never put a server IP or other literal infrastructure address in a rule file.

## Commands (Windows, PowerShell, from repo root)
- Run the stack: `npm run dev` (docker: mysql, api, soketi), then `npm run dev:web:local` for the frontend.
- Tests: `npm test` (smoke), `npm run test:backend`, `npm run test:frontend`, `npm run test:all`. Scenario runners for the active modules: `test:team-access`, `test:e-approval`. `npm run test:list` shows all of them.
- Frontend checks: `cd frontend; npm run lint; npm run typecheck`. Backend format: `cd backend; php vendor/bin/pint --dirty`.
- Artisan: on the host `cd backend; php artisan ...`, or in the container `node scripts/compose-run.js --env-file .env.docker exec api php artisan ...`.
- PowerShell syntax only (use `;`, not `&&`). Ask before `npm run dev:fresh` (wipes the local database) or anything that removes Docker volumes.

## Non-negotiables
1. Tenant isolation: every query, job, cache key, broadcast channel and file path is tenant-scoped. Cross-tenant access must be impossible, not just unlikely.
2. Every endpoint authorizes and validates. The four active modules do this in the controller: `abort_unless($request->user()?->can('<module>:<resource>:<action>'), 403)`, then `$request->validate([...])`, then a Service, then `AbstractApiController` (`ok`, `created`, `okWithMeta`). They do not use FormRequest, Policy or API Resource classes. Copy the module you are in.
3. Business rules live in Services (`<Module><Thing>Service`, base in `app/Core/Services`). Repositories are optional (`app/Core/Repositories`). Never put business rules in controllers, models or React components.
4. No credentials in code or repo. Never read `.env*` files. Config comes from env / secrets manager.
5. Critical actions write an audit log entry (who, what, tenant, before/after).
6. UUID (ordered/v7) primary keys.
7. Production-grade code only: real error handling and logging. Factories, seeders and test doubles inside tests are fine. Placeholder or demo code in app code is not.
8. No duplicated logic. Reuse existing Core classes, module services, hooks and UI components before creating new ones.

## UI work (any file under `frontend/`)
Follow @ui-theme.mdc first, then @ui-data-and-forms.mdc and @ui-accessibility.mdc. Use the tokens and variants already in `frontend/app/globals.css` and `components/ui` (see `docs/design-system`). Every screen needs loading, empty and error states and must work in light and dark.

## How to work
- Match the size of the answer to the size of the request. No folder trees, schema dumps or long step-by-step essays for small changes. Use `/new-feature` when a full deliverable is needed.
- Before writing code, read the relevant rule, the module's doc in `docs/`, and copy the conventions of the closest existing module (backend and frontend).
- Definition of done: relevant tests pass (`npm run test:backend` / `test:frontend`), `lint` and `typecheck` pass, Pint applied, and `node scripts/ui-drift.mjs` passes for any frontend change. New endpoints have an authorization test and a cross-tenant test. Report what you actually ran and the results.
- Ask before: destructive migrations, adding dependencies, changing auth, tenancy, Docker or CI config.

